  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "Each pushbutton straddles the breadboard centre gap. Side 1 (1.l/1.r) is in the top half and goes to the 5V rail (tp). Side 2 (2.l/2.r) is in the bottom half.",
  "Each signal wire goes to the bottom-half column of 2.l. The 10k pull-down sits in the 2.r column, from the bottom-half strip to the GND rail (bn). Both columns are on the same side of the button, so the input pin and its pull-down are on the same side, as the tutorial says.",
  "Leonardo pins 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 go to buttons 1 to 5 in that order, as in the schematic.",
  "Rails: the 5V wire goes to tp.1 and the five button feeds go to tp.2 to tp.6, all one strip. The GND wire goes to bn.1 and the resistors go to bn.2 to bn.6, all one strip.",
  "Breadboard hole positions are my own layout, since the circuit photo did not load. The schematic fixes the electrical connections."
